{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-year-nonhaptog-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.73, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-year-nonhaptog`: the Year twin of `scale-county-idle-nonhaptog` -- its selections unchanged (NonHAPTOG, 88, and its mechanism, 3000, at running and start exhaust, extended idle, auxiliary power and crankcase running, start and extended idle, with NMOG, the fourteen integrated species, and THC, NMHC and VOC at the rated processes), under `scale-county-timeagg-year`'s collapse: January, April, July and October 2020, both day types, all 24 hours, road types 1 and 4, source types 21 and 62, `inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`, `<aggregateBy key=\"Year\"/>` and `<outputtimestep value=\"Year\"/>`. MOVESOutput is 33,876 rows.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is TOGSpeciationCalculator after PreAggYEAR.sql: NonHAPTOG is NMOG minus the integrated species on the FINISHED quantities, so the toxics' second months'-share factor (AirToxicsCalculator's raw FuelSupply sum, F70) enters the subtraction while NMOG's does not; and, as at Hour, MOVES writes 88 at every process the mechanism is selected on, a pollutant-process or not.\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1; `db_aggregationmonth` and `db_rateday` are read from its XML by `tools/runspec-month-selection.py` and `tools/runspec-day-selection.py`. `n_outputRate` is bound to 33876; `n_physicsRow` 21, the two source types' physics rows.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "air-toxics",
      "hc-speciation",
      "crankcase",
      "nonhaptog",
      "mechanism",
      "start-exhaust",
      "running-exhaust",
      "time-aggregation",
      "output-time-step",
      "year-aggregation"
    ]
  },
